{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"851bb9f0-451f-42ce-8085-0aa631dd1583","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The cause of the missing notifications has been identified and resolved. Details have been documented in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-XVmpvh/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Causes\n1. **Fatal Zsh Error on Read-Only Variable**: In `zsh`, `status` is a built-in read-only variable (an alias for `$?`). In [`bin/nightly-review.zsh`](file:///tmp/h-XVmpvh/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L19), attempting to assign `status=$?` immediately after `claude` caused `zsh` to terminate the script with a fatal error: `read-only variable: status`.\n2. **Failure Handling Never Reached**: Even though `claude` failed (due to authentication `Not logged in · Please run /login`), the subsequent `if [ $status -ne 0 ]` check and error notifier (`$NOTIFY \"nightly review FAILED...\"`) were never executed because the script aborted on the assignment.\n\n### Fix\n- Updated [`bin/nightly-review.zsh`](file:///tmp/h-XVmpvh/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L18-L24) to use `exit_code` instead of the reserved `status` variable.\n- Documented findings in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-XVmpvh/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":121.60323700000001,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":221702,"output_tokens":2696,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":556310,"total_tokens":224398}}}
